<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- BETA build variant.
     ====================
     Identical to manifest.xml apart from this comment block and two attributes:

       id   - a SEPARATE application id. The INTENT is that the beta installs
              ALONGSIDE the production app instead of replacing it, and that a
              ride recorded with both fields active carries two independently
              attributed copies of the schema below.

              That is the design PREMISE of this file, not a measured fact.
              Nobody in this repo has installed both apps on a device or looked
              at a decoded .FIT file. Tracked as #64 (FIT attribution, with
              byte-exact pass criteria) and #63 (whether two application ids
              really keep separate settings - the one piece of local evidence,
              the SDK simulator keying its .SET file by .prg FILE NAME, points
              the other way). Do not restate either as fact until one of those
              issues is closed with evidence. See README.md, "Settings: what is
              known, and what is not".
       name - "@Strings.AppNameBeta" so the two entries are intended to be
              distinguishable in the device's data-field picker. The rendered
              on-device label is likewise unobserved (#63).

     The FIT developer field ids stay 0-3, exactly as production
     (source/CarbBurnView.mc:127-134). Keeping the schema identical is what an
     A/B diff of one activity would need; renumbering here would make the two
     sets incomparable no matter how attribution turns out. So: do not
     renumber, and do not add a beta-only field.

     The <iq:products> list MUST stay identical to manifest.xml. Partially
     enforced: monkeyc exits 102 when -d names a product a manifest omits, so
     CI's per-device loop catches anything MISSING from this list. Nothing
     catches a product added to one manifest and not the other outside
     env.DEVICES - that is the #46 gap, now spanning two manifests.

     This id was not registered on the Connect IQ Store by this project, and
     must never be submitted there. (Whether some unrelated app already holds
     it is not checkable from here - there is no store account.) It exists for
     sideloading a beta next to the store build.
-->
<iq:manifest xmlns:iq="http://www.garmin.com/xml/connectiq" version="3">
    <iq:application entry="CarbBurnApp"
                    id="3aa0137493fa4511ba559720835b1ab5"
                    launcherIcon="@Drawables.LauncherIcon"
                    minApiLevel="3.1.0"
                    name="@Strings.AppNameBeta"
                    type="datafield">
        <iq:products>
            <iq:product id="edge530"/>
            <iq:product id="edge830"/>
            <iq:product id="edge540"/>
            <iq:product id="edge840"/>
            <iq:product id="edge1030"/>
            <iq:product id="edge1030plus"/>
            <iq:product id="edge1040"/>
            <iq:product id="edge1050"/>
            <iq:product id="edgeexplore2"/>
            <iq:product id="fenix6pro"/>
            <iq:product id="fenix7"/>
            <iq:product id="fenix8pro47mm"/>
            <iq:product id="fr955"/>
        </iq:products>
        <iq:permissions>
            <iq:uses-permission id="FitContributor"/>
        </iq:permissions>
        <iq:languages>
            <iq:language>eng</iq:language>
        </iq:languages>
    </iq:application>
</iq:manifest>
